  "mechanism": {
    "description": "One separate, identically configured client launch whose ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL points at a loopback recorder started by the tool. The recorded request body is the exact model input the client built, so every active instruction source is enumerated from the client's own project-memory labels and proved byte-exact against the file on disk. The project-memory block is recognised by the sentence 'Codebase and user instructions are shown below.', which 2.1.220 placed under a '# claudeMd' heading and a clean 2.1.302 CLI launch emits without one.",
